{"agent":"buglane5","data":{"body":"The ddflow lanes state table shows ITEM/STATE/HEARTBEAT/FOR but not WHICH pipeline step a lane is on: for a working lane an operator cannot see whether it is on research or unit_tests without reading its brief. The Lane model already carries mid_gate (a gate.started with no later outcome) and last_event_kind for a stopped lane; extend it to a per-lane current step (the in-flight or next unsatisfied gate of the held item, else the last event kind) and render it as a STEP column in ddflow lanes (state), carried in the lane as_dict wire for CLI and MCP parity. ETA stays the ETA-surfaces tasks concern (P-eta). Tests first.","globs":["ddflow/services/lanes/render.py","ddflow/services/lanes/ledger.py","tests/test_lanes_state_step.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"P-coordination","priority":60,"tags":["dx","coordination","no-deps"],"title":"ddflow lanes state: a STEP column naming the gate each lane is on"},"id":"eddd92e6f1924b6145d1bb475","kind":"task.added","lamport":190527,"schema":1,"subject":"LN-lanes-state-step","ts":"2026-11-13T05:40:14.149163Z"}
